course: dictionary
lesson: 4376
title: One small word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word ha is only two letters, but it can do different jobs. In a story it is usually a sound. «Ha!» can show a character laughing, or being proud when they have won. Ask yourself who is speaking and how they feel.
explain: Written as «ha ha», it shows laughing. The words around it tell you whether the laugh is happy or unkind. «Haha, you're so dumb» just makes someone go quiet, because a laugh can hurt.
explain: Ha also has a short written job: it is short for hectare, a unit of land. 1 ha is 10000 square metres, a square 100 m by 100 m. You will see it on maps, at farms, forests and parks. Context tells you which meaning is right.
fact: «Ha» is a sound people make when they laugh, or when they are surprised or have won.
fact: «Ha ha» written down shows laughing.
fact: ha is short for hectare: 1 ha is 10000 square metres, a square 100 m by 100 m.
fact: In Python, multiplying text by a number repeats it: print('ha' * 3) prints hahaha.
fact: Context decides the meaning: in a story ha is usually a sound, but on a map of a park it can mean hectares.
exercise: «Ha!» shouted Sam, as the ball hit the back of the net. What does the ha show? | Sam is asking a question | Sam is measuring the field | *Sam is pleased, having won | Sam is sad and crying
exercise: The map says the park is 5 ha. What does ha mean here? | A kind of bird | A laugh | A question | *Hectares, a unit of land
exercise: «Haha, you're so dumb» is said to a friend. What does this laugh do to the friend? | It makes them hungry | It makes them fall asleep | It makes them jump for joy | *It makes them go quiet and feel hurt
test: In Python, what does print('ha' * 3) show? | *hahaha | 9 | 'ha' | ha3
test: How many square metres is 1 ha? | *10000 | 100000 | 100 | 1000
exam: What does «ha ha» written in a comic usually show? | *Laughing | Crying | Counting | Walking
